@startuml
' Derived from src/nonogram/admin/book_manager.py:50 (BookStatus),
' :2223 (set_book_status, the ONE transition method), :2180 (the readiness gate),
' :488 (_draft_after_membership_change) and src/nonogram/db/models.py:142.
title AGG-002 Book — five states, one transition method, one gate

[*] --> draft : create\n(books.status default='draft')

state draft {
  state "general info · print spec (Book 1 profile, CON-018)\nplan (DEFAULT_PLAN = 150 at 40/40/20)\nselect puzzles by longest-side tab\narrange within a level" as work
}

state "the readiness gate\n_refuse_unless_the_planned_book(...)" as gate <<choice>>

draft --> gate : set_book_status(anything but draft)
gate --> ready_for_pdf : every plan cell within\nREADY_TOLERANCE_POINTS = 3 (inclusive)
gate --> draft : ready_refusal names EVERY\noffending cell at once (AC-221)\nor NO_PLAN_REFUSAL

ready_for_pdf --> pdf_generated
pdf_generated --> ready_for_kdp
ready_for_kdp --> published

published --> [*] : terminal — set_book_status raises\nValueError("Cannot change status of published book")

' INV-012, book_manager.py:488
ready_for_pdf --> draft : membership change\n(_draft_after_membership_change)
pdf_generated --> draft : membership change
ready_for_kdp --> draft : membership change
ready_for_pdf --> draft : save_plan (:773)

note right of gate
  Runs at the EXIT FROM DRAFT, not continuously
  (book_manager.py:2237). INV-012's return-to-draft
  is what pays for it again, so a KDP upload is never
  built from a book that no longer matches its plan.

  The comparison is integer-only, to avoid float drift:
    abs(actual[c] - planned[c]) * 100
        > READY_TOLERANCE_POINTS * plan.count
end note

note bottom
  Also refused by set_book_status, before the gate:
    - an unknown status                -> ValueError("Invalid status: ...")
    - an empty selection, target != draft -> ValueError("Must have puzzles before advancing status")

  INV-008: a change to a PUBLISHED book's membership needs explicit
  confirmation — AddOutcome/RemoveOutcome carry a `confirmed` flag and
  the route answers 409 (app.py:2875).

  In DB mode the check and the write are NOT atomic: the row is read and
  judged in one session and written in another. book_manager.py:2247
  records that the exposure is the whole DB layer's rather than this
  method's, and that it is accepted because the panel is a single-user
  loopback tool (CON-015) served by gunicorn --workers 1.
end note

@enduml
